Looking at this problem, I need to find the largest n such that the diagonals of a regular n-gon can be 2-colored with no monochromatic triangle (where a "triangle" means three vertices pairwise connected by diagonals, i.e., three pairwise non-adjacent vertices).

## Proof

**Answer: n = 11.**

### Construction for n = 11

Label vertices 0, 1, ..., 10. For each diagonal {i, j}, let d = min(|i−j|, 11−|i−j|) ∈ {2, 3, 4, 5} be the cyclic distance. Color the diagonal **blue** if d ∈ {2, 3} and **black** if d ∈ {4, 5}.

Any three pairwise non-adjacent vertices have gaps (g₁, g₂, g₃) with each gᵢ ≥ 2 and g₁ + g₂ + g₃ = 11. The edge type of each gap is dᵢ = min(gᵢ, 11−gᵢ). The possible gap multisets and resulting edge-type/color multisets are:

| Gap multiset | Edge types | Colors |
|---|---|---|
| {2, 2, 7} | {2, 2, 4} | {blue, blue, black} |
| {2, 3, 6} | {2, 3, 5} | {blue, blue, black} |
| {2, 4, 5} | {2, 4, 5} | {blue, black, black} |
| {3, 3, 5} | {3, 3, 5} | {blue, blue, black} |
| {3, 4, 4} | {3, 4, 4} | {blue, black, black} |

In every case, the three edges are **not all the same color**, so no monochromatic triangle exists. (Any ordering of a gap multiset produces the same multiset of edge types, hence the same color multiset.) ∎

### Impossibility for n ≥ 12

For n ≥ 12, consider the six vertices {0, 2, 4, 6, 8, 10}. Every pair differs by an even number, so no pair is adjacent in Cₙ (adjacency requires cyclic distance 1). Since the maximum difference is 10 and n ≥ 12, the cyclic distance between any two of these vertices is at least 2. Therefore **all 15 edges between these six vertices are diagonals** of the n-gon, and they are all colored.

These six vertices induce a complete graph K₆ in the diagonal graph. By the Ramsey number **R(3,3) = 6**, every 2-coloring of the edges of K₆ contains a monochromatic triangle. This monochromatic triangle consists of three diagonals of the same color connecting three vertices — violating the condition.

Therefore no valid coloring exists for n ≥ 12.

### Conclusion

The largest possible value of n is **11**.

